Definitions:

"Bitcoin Protocol" means the protocol as defined by the original Bitcoin White Paper published on 31 October 2008 by Satoshi Nakamoto titled "Bitcoin: A Peer-to-Peer Electronic Cash System" ("Bitcoin White Paper"), including:
(a) consensus mechanisms for the blockchain protocol; and
(b) consensus mechanisms for the peer-to-peer protocol for interaction between nodes; but
(c) excluding any applications that use the protocol.

"BSV Blockchains" means any blockchain implementation that implements and uses the Bitcoin Protocol.

"Network Access Rules" means rules set by BSV Blockchains for governing relationships between nodes based on Bitcoin Protocol rules.

"Software" means the software distributed under this license.

